---
title: Welcome
description: Learn how to configure feature flags in the Vonage Video iOS App.
---

Welcome! In this tutorial you will configure the **Vonage Video iOS App** (`vonage-video-ios-app`), a Swift application built with [Tuist](https://tuist.io). Building and running it natively requires **Xcode 26+**, **Tuist**, and **SwiftLint** on **macOS** — none of which this Codespace has. So instead of editing and building here, you will clone the repo to your own Mac and do all of that work there.

This Codespace's only job is to run the shared Node.js backend server that the iOS app talks to, and to expose its port so your locally-running app can reach it.

## In this tutorial you will

- Start the shared backend server in this Codespace and make its port public
- Clone `vonage-video-ios-app` to your own machine and run it in Xcode against that backend
- Explore how feature flags are structured in `VERA/Config/app-config.json`
- Edit feature flags and regenerate the corresponding Swift configuration
- Rebuild the app and confirm your changes in the iOS Simulator

{% aside type="caution" %}
This Codespace does not include Xcode or macOS. You cannot build, run, or preview the iOS app here — everything you do in this Codespace is limited to running the backend server. Building and verifying the app happens in Xcode on your own Mac.
{% /aside %}

{% aside %}
Looking to customize colors, typography, or shape instead? See the companion **Vonage Video iOS App Theme Customization** tutorial.
{% /aside %}

Let's start by setting up the backend server and getting the app running locally.
